"## My solver conventions · checked against the current code\n- **Frames:** \\(T_{AB}\\) maps B into A; vertices are T_WC. The frontend returns T_ji; the graph stores its inverse Z_ij.\n- **Graph residual:** \\(r_{ij}=\\operatorname{Log}(Z_{ij}^{-1}T_i^{-1}T_j)\\). Twists are [rho, phi]; updates multiply on the LEFT.\n- **Two Jacobians:** Edge-information point residual p_j − q gives \\([-I,\\hat q]\\) (3×6). A graph edge has two 6×6 endpoint Jacobians, effectively \\(J_i=-\\operatorname{Ad}(T_j^{-1})\\), \\(J_j=+\\operatorname{Ad}(T_j^{-1})\\) in the current code.\n- **Unfinished detail:** right_jacobian() returns identity. The full derivative includes the inverse right Jacobian of Log; see Math details.\n- **Actual solve:** Huber weighting, fixed vertex 0, dense assembly then sparse SimplicialLDLT. The configured run uses LM, with diagonal damping \\(H+\\lambda(\\operatorname{diag}(H)+10^{-6}I)\\).\n\n"
